gabrielle: quick PSA — trying to make the JS SDK play nice across Node (CJS), ESM bundlers, and edge runtimes. local app works but our edge example fails during deploy with `TypeError: sdk.default is not a function`.
ravi: that's usually an export interop problem. Do you have your package.json exports + main/module typed out?
gabrielle: current minimal package.json excerpt: ```json
"main": "dist/cjs/index.js",
"module": "dist/esm/index.js",
"types": "dist/types/index.d.ts",
"exports": {".": {"import": "./dist/esm/index.js","require": "./dist/cjs/index.js"}}
```
li: two issues here: 1) bundlers/edge runners sometimes follow `module`/`browser`/`worker` conditions rather than plain `import`, 2) TS resolution can pick wrong `.d.ts` if `types` is not listed in subpath exports.
anya: also check whether your ESM build actually emits a default export. Many toolchains output only named exports which breaks `import SDK from` patterns used in older examples.
gabrielle: confirmed — our ESM output only has named exports, and our CJS build adds `module.exports.default = createClient` for compat. That's why edge (esbuild) which prefers ESM ends up with no default.
ravi: pragmatic fixes: a) emit `export default createClient` in ESM build, or b) add an explicit worker/edge subpath in exports so edge consumers import a guaranteed ESM file. Example: ```json
"exports": {
  "./edge": {"import": "./dist/esm/edge.js","types": "./dist/types/edge.d.ts"},
  ".": {"import": "./dist/esm/index.js","require": "./dist/cjs/index.js"}
}
```
li: and add types to the `./edge` subpath. TS often resolves wrong declaration for subpaths if types aren't listed there. Also consider `typesVersions` mapping for older TS.
gabrielle: another annoying behavior — retry logic in the edge example drains request bodies on the second attempt (we pass a ReadableStream as body from callers). Node clones OK, worker env fails.
anya: worker ReadableStreams cannot always be cloned. Solutions: buffer the body (ArrayBuffer/Uint8Array) for retries, or change retry helper to accept a factory `() => RequestInit` so each attempt gets fresh body.
ravi: sample helper pattern: ```js
async function retryFetch(makeInit, attempts = 2) {
  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {
    const init = typeof makeInit === 'function' ? makeInit() : makeInit;
    const res = await fetch('/api', init);
    if (res.ok) return res;
  }
  throw new Error('failed');
}
```
li: also add a tiny `ensureRetryableBody(init)` util in SDK to auto-buffer when in a worker and body is a stream; keep it opt-in to avoid copying for large uploads. Document cost tradeoffs.
gabrielle: good points. CI pain: jest in monorepo chokes on ESM in node_modules for packages that publish a mixed tree. Tests failed on CI for the samples.
li: our usual approach: publish compiled CJS under `dist/cjs` and keep a `jest` stanza or pretest CI step to transpile ESM samples. Alternatively add `exports` with a `node` condition to point to CJS for older tools: ```json
"exports": { ".": { "node": { "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js" }, "default": "./dist/esm/index.js" } }
```
anya: also add tiny `examples/edge` and `examples/node` in repo and include CI smoke jobs that deploy edge example to Vercel/Cloudflare to catch runtime mismatches early.
devx-bot: created issue DX-3150: "sdk: add edge subpath + ESM default + retry-safe body helper + examples" assigned to @gabrielle.
ci-bot: note: CI job `examples-smoke` failed on previous run; will re-run when PR linked.
gabrielle: action items I will take: 1) change build to emit ESM default export and named exports, 2) add `./edge` conditional export with `types` subpath, 3) implement opt-in `ensureRetryableBody` + document factory pattern, 4) add `examples/edge` and CI smoke. I'll open a PR with a minimal repro and link the Vercel deploy preview.
ravi: when you do, include a short README section with recommended import patterns per runtime: Node (require/import), Next Edge (import from 'sdk/edge' or use named exports), Cloudflare (import './edge' and avoid streaming bodies unless buffered).
li: and add `typesVersions` for older TS if you're seeing users with 3rd-party tooling not following `exports` correctly.
gabrielle: thanks all — will ping here with the PR. :thumbsup:
